hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"300","Na, na, Ibrahim bin Munqidh bin Abdullah Al-Khawlani, Ayoub bin Suwayd told us, Yunus bin Yazid told us, Al-Zuhri told me, Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar told me, he said: Omar used to say in the mosque at the top of his voice: “Avoid idle talk in the mosque.” He said Abdullah bin Omar: “I spent the night in the mosque during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was a young single boy, and the dogs used to urinate And you come and turn around in the mosque, and they did not sprinkle any of that.” Abu Bakr said: This means urinating outside the mosque, and turning back and forth in the mosque after urinating."
